  <data name="Settings_Ai_SaveKey.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Save key</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_Capabilities_Help.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Verify capabilities separately. Tests use synthetic prompts, never container data or app actions.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_TestCapabilities.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Test capabilities</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_CancelTest.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cancel test</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_Permissions_Header.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Container AI Assistant permissions</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_Permissions_Help.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Read-only tools always run automatically. For every other tool, turn its switch on to let the assistant run it without asking. Anything left off will prompt you for approval each time.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AllowDelete.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Allow the assistant to delete things</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AllowDelete.OffContent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Off — it cannot delete</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AllowDelete.OnContent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>On — it can delete</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AllowDelete_Help.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Off by default. Until you turn this on, the assistant cannot remove containers, volumes or networks, or delete Kubernetes resources — it will say the action is turned off instead of asking. Removing a volume destroys the data in it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AutoApprove.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Let the assistant act without asking</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AutoApprove.OffContent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Ask me first (recommended)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AutoApprove.OnContent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Never ask</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_AutoApprove_Help.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Skips every prompt, including the Compose review that the switches below cannot turn off. It only waives asking — it does not grant deleting, and plans the app cannot apply safely are still refused. Everything still appears in Activity.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_Perm.OffContent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Require approval</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Settings_Ai_Perm.OnContent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Run automatically</value>
  </data>
